ss=\"1\">1: \u003Cspan>Orsi: ΠΙΣΤ; lapis: the initial vertical does not join the upper horizontal, and the spacing is too narrow for Π, whereas the upper bar of the Τ is simply lost on the right\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\u003Cbr>\u003C/li>\u003Cli>\u003Cspan class=\"3\">3: \u003Cspan>Trace of a horizontal forming the upper part of a letter such as Γ, Τ, Π\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\u003C/li>\u003C/ul>",{"id":222,"html":223},"translation","\u003Ch2> translation\u003C/h2>\u003Cp class=\"translation-author\">  \u003C/p>\u003Cp>  \u003C/p>",{"id":225,"html":226},"commentary","\u003Ch2>commentary\u003C/h2>  \u003Cp>The large omicron and the horizontal outer bar of the sigma suggest a date after 200 BCE, and the size of the letters suggests some sort of monumental text, but without a more detailed provenance than simply 'Epipolai', little more can be said, except that this is a rare surviving instance of public epigraphy from later Hellenistic Syracusae.\u003C/p>  ",{"id":228,"html":229},"bibliography","\u003Ch2>bibliography\u003C/h2>  \u003Cul>\u003Cli> Orsi 1889 386 \u003Ca href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001711\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001711\u003C/a>  \u003C/li>\u003Cli> Orsi 2018 Tacc. 1, p.51 \u003Ca href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10002617\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10002617\u003C/a>\u003C/li>\u003C/ul>  \u003Cul>\u003Cli>\u003C/li>\u003C/ul>  ",{"id":231,"html":232},"handnote","\u003Cp>Tall wide, plainly v-cut letters with very slight wedge serifs at the terminals.\u003C/p> Line 1  75  Line 2  70-73  Interlineation line 1 to 2  20  Interlineation line 2 to 3  20  ",{"id":234,"html":235},"license"," Licensed under a Creative Commons-Attribution 4.0 licence. ",[237,239,242,243],{"html":238},"Text encoding: Jonathan Prag; edition source: autopsy Prag 2016-10-11, magazzino B, cassette 37",{"id":240,"lang":137,"html":241},"edition-interpretive","\u003Cdiv class=\"textpart\" lang=\"grc\